  <!-- EN: lessonIntro-&gt;After so many sleepless nights of careful deliberation, I came to a simple conclussion: -->
  <!-- EN: lessonIntro-&gt;What is a fundamental truth of human existence? -->
  <!-- EN: lessonIntro-&gt;I have suffered a lot in this life. But this suffering has taught me a simple principle: -->
  <!-- EN: lessonIntro-&gt;Growing in squalor on the [place_summary] [place_name], I learned a sincere axiom: -->
  <!-- EN: lessonIntro-&gt;Internalize this lesson, for it will serve you well: -->
  <!-- EN: lessonIntro-&gt;Are you feeling lost? Perhaps you haven&apos;t yet figured out this very simple concept: -->
  <!-- EN: lessonIntro-&gt;They tried to tempt me with a life of rich, dull productivity, but they couldn&apos;t fool me: -->
  <!-- EN: lessonMain-&gt;pleasure, the satisfaction of bodily desires, is the highest good and proper aim of human life. Whether through religion or philosophy our entire lives should be focused on enjoying ourselves as much as possible -->
  <!-- EN: lessonMain-&gt;I finally figured out the only reason to be alive is to enjoy it -->
  <!-- EN: lessonMain-&gt;the only way to get rid of temptation is to yield to it -->
  <!-- EN: lessonMain-&gt;salvation is for the feeble. I don&apos;t want salvation, I want life, all of life, the miserable as well as the superb -->
  <!-- EN: lessonMain-&gt;pleasure is not a need, but an incentive -->
  <!-- EN: lessonMain-&gt;the most responsible way of life right now is to enjoy ourselves while we can -->
  <!-- EN: lessonMain-&gt;you can live to be a hundred if you give up all the things that make you want to live to be a hundred -->
  <!-- EN: lessonReinforcement-&gt;No one can argue with that. -->
  <!-- EN: lessonReinforcement-&gt;Only fools think otherwise. -->
  <!-- EN: lessonReinforcement-&gt;And as we now know, that was soon to become evident to everyone. -->
  <!-- EN: lessonReinforcement-&gt;Everything that has happened since has reinforced that fact. -->
  <!-- EN: lessonReinforcement-&gt;It is as if that is etched directly into my mind. -->
  <!-- EN: lessonReinforcement-&gt;It is something I&apos;ll never forget. -->
